cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  dMRI Rosetta Stone: a controlled comparison of diffusion tensor
  estimators across FSL, MRtrix3 and DIPY
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata
  from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Busra
    family-names: Mutlu Ipek
    affiliation: King's College London
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8983-7277'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/happybrotherhood/dmri-rosetta-stone'
abstract: >-
  A container that runs FSL, MRtrix3 and DIPY on byte-identical diffusion
  MRI data, with the scripts that compare their tensor fits. Shows that FSL
  --wls and MRtrix3 -iter 0 return matching tensors, that the toolkits
  differ mainly in the estimator they apply by default, and that
  measured-signal weighting is the most biased scheme in anisotropic
  tissue (Rician-noise phantoms and simulations on the real gradient
  tables).
keywords:
  - diffusion MRI
  - diffusion tensor
  - weighted least squares
  - FSL
  - MRtrix3
  - DIPY
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
